  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "1.\tThe proposed development, by reason of its scale, bulk, mass, siting and foot print, would result in the loss of green open space and thereby fails to provide a high quality design response which has regard to the pattern and grain of existing spaces and that contributes to a positive relationship between the urban structure and natural landscape features. As such the proposal would be contrary to policies 7.4 and 7B(e) and 2.18 of the Adopted Ealing Development Management DPD (2013), Policy 1.1 (i) of the Adopted Core Strategy (2012) and policies 2.18, 7.4, 7.6 and 7.18 of the Consolidated London Plan (2015). | 2.\tThe proposed development, would result in the loss of characteristic space and mature trees of amenity value as well as the bulk, scale, mass and footprint of the development resulting in a dominant and overbearing development along this section of The Park, thereby failing to preserve and enhance the character and appearance of the Ealing Green Conservation Area. As such the proposal would be contrary to the Ealing Green Conservation Area Management Plan (2008), policies 7.4, 7B(e) and 7C and 2.18 of the Adopted Ealing Development Management DPD (2013), policy 1.1 (g) and (h) and 1.2 (g) of the Adopted Core Strategy (2012) and policies 7.4, 7.6, 7.8 and 7.21 of the Consolidated London Plan (2015)."
  ],
